# VeraProb — Frontend Rules (Dart/Flutter)

You are editing Frontend files. Adhere to the standards defined in `AGENTS.md` and `.kiro/steering/ux-standards.md`.

- **Clean Architecture:** `lib/features/` must never import concrete classes from `lib/infrastructure/` (except `observability/` or `config/`).
- **Clean UI & Opaque Error Handling:**
  - **No Raw Exceptions in UI (UX-RAW-EXCEPTION):** Never display `$e`, `e.toString()`, or state wrappers (`${actionState.error}`, `${asyncValue.error}`) in SnackBars/Text. Map errors to domain vocabulary.
  - **No IIFE in UI (IIFE-UI-SMELL):** Never use Immediately Invoked Function Expressions `() { ... }()` inside `build` methods or `switch` statements. Extract complex logic to helper methods (`_buildX`).
  - **Accent-fill Contrast (ACCENT-FILL-CONTRAST):** Foreground on primary/secondary/error accent fills is always `VeraProbColors.background` (dark), never `Colors.white` (fails WCAG AA 4.5:1).
  - **Wasm Context Leaks (WASM-CONTEXT-LEAK):** Capture `ScaffoldMessenger.of(context)` or `Navigator.of(context)` BEFORE any `await`.
  - **UI Nesting & Local State:** Avoid redundant Column/Row nesting and single-use widget wrappers. Keep local UI states (active tabs, search query input, panel toggles) in widget-local state (StatefulWidget/hooks); do not pollute Riverpod global graph with UI-local state. Extract widgets to `shared/` only if used in 3+ distinct screens (Rule of Three).
- **Formatting:** Use UTF-8 with LF (`\n`) line endings exclusively. Resolve static warnings and unused code via `dart fix --apply`.
